__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.so
*.egg
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
*.log
.env
.venv
venv/
data/*
!data/README.md
# audit trail stays in git (small text/json only - never the rasters)
!data/dem_links.json
!data/evidence/
!data/evidence/**
!data/reconstructed/
!data/reconstructed/provenance.json
# small REAL-data dev fixture (few MB, int16-quantised) - see scripts/make_dev_fixture.py
!data/fixture/
!data/fixture/**
# official competition rasters, runner-downloaded and sha256-pinned (git bridge;
# the 418,912,844 B feature stack is committed as ~90 MiB parts because GitHub
# rejects blobs >= 100 MB) - see scripts/assemble_data_bridge.py
!data/bridge/
!data/bridge/**
# GEMSDOE4 (2026-09-25): the ~418 MB of *.part-* blobs are restored locally by
# scripts/fetch_bridge_parts.py and are never committed here - this platform caps a
# turn's patchset at ~128 MB.  The manifest and the mirror record stay tracked.
data/bridge/*.part-*
!data/*.md
outputs/
outputs_recon/
outputs_*/
*.tif
*.tiff
!data/fixture/*.tif
!data/bridge/*.tif
# GEMSDOE4 new-fault-first line (2026-09-25): the NFF probability fields and the union artifact are
# the *inputs* scripts/combine_newfault.py reads back to reproduce
# data/evidence/combined/submission.tif byte for byte, so they are evidence, not scratch output.
# the SGMC/QFaults proxy truth rasters: fixed evidence the scoring workflows read back, and small
!data/evidence/proxy/proxy_catalogue.tif
!data/evidence/xcat/qfaults_catalogue.tif
!data/evidence/newfault/*/prob_raw.tif
!data/evidence/newfault/*/submission.tif
!data/evidence/combined/submission.tif
# GEMSDOE4 session 34: the clean-pool CONTROL artifact.  The union evidence section of the site
# and docs/SESSION34_PROTOCOL.md both point at it as the arm with no in-sample member, and a
# control that exists only in a report is a claim rather than evidence - same rule as above.
!data/evidence/combined_clean/submission.tif
# GEMSDOE4 session 31 (2026-09-25): the rejected 6-member / leave-one-out candidate rasters and
# the adopted contrast measurement are evidence - they record how the shipping decision was made
!data/evidence/union6/submission.tif
!data/evidence/union6_loo/**/submission.tif
# GEMSDOE4 session 31 follow-up (2026-09-26): the deep-ensemble member raster is 571 KB, is
# sha256-pinned by data/evidence/combined/report.json (7f00890a...) and by its own sidecar, and
# tests/test_field_selection.py scores against it - leaving it untracked made those tests ERROR
# at setup on every fresh checkout (CI had been running with 3 collection errors since before
# PR #2).  It is evidence with a pin, so it travels in git like the other identity rasters.
!data/evidence/runs/ens12-adopted-floor0.1-w0/submission.tif
# GEMSDOE4 session 32 (2026-09-26): proxy_only diversity member + LOO re-adoption of the
# union.  The classical baseline submission.tif is a union member (sha pin 9f2577cf…) and
# must travel in git so combine_newfault can re-run from a fresh clone; the proxy_only
# member and the LOO candidate rasters are the evidence the adoption decision rests on.
!data/evidence/baseline/submission.tif
!data/evidence/union_po/submission.tif
!data/evidence/union_po_loo/**/submission.tif
# GEMSDOE4 session 34 (2026-09-26): a paired adoption contrast has to name the raster it compares
# AGAINST, and `data/evidence/union_po_loo/prev_committed_*.tif` is that reference (session 33's
# prev_committed_nff_union5.tif, this session's prev_committed_nff_k2_t0.18.tif).  If the reference
# does not travel in git, `scripts/paired_union_contrast.py` cannot re-run from a fresh clone and the
# contrast JSON cites a path no reviewer can open - the same "audit artefact must be committed or
# not cited" rule this repository keeps applying to itself.
!data/evidence/union_po_loo/prev_committed_*.tif
*.zip
*.gdb
*.grd
*.csv
!docs/data_catalog.csv
!data/evidence/*.csv
*.pt
*.pth
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.venv/
.venv/
